  "meta-description": "Build a cleaning quote form that prices each home by its rooms and extras and keeps every request in a database you own. Free to start.",
  "description": "Build a cleaning quote form that prices each home from its rooms and extras and saves every request to a database you own.",
  "acrm---key-feature-sub-heading": "These six pieces turn a customer's answers into a price, or into a site walk when the job is too big to price from a form.",
  "acrm---key-feature-4-content": "<h3>Large jobs held for a site walk</h3><p>Pick the square footage where a form price stops being safe. A request over that line shows no price and goes on the owner's list for a site walk, with the address attached.</p>",
  "acrm---key-feature-5-content": "<h3>Each request in an email or Slack</h3><p>Choose who hears about a new request and where: an email to the owner or a post in a Slack channel. The message carries the address and the total the customer saw on screen.</p>",
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Cleaning Quote Form FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a cleaning quote form?\", \"a\": \"A cleaning quote form is the request a cleaning business puts on its website so customers can ask for a price. It collects the size of the home or building and the type of clean wanted. The answers either produce a price on screen or give the owner what they need to send one.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a cleaning quote form?\", \"a\": \"Write down your prices first: the base rate by home size and every extra. Then describe the form and those prices to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. It builds the form and the database behind it, and any price can be changed later by asking.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions should a cleaning quote form ask?\", \"a\": \"Ask what sets the price. Start with the type of clean and the size of the home, then the visit schedule and any extras. Add the address and a phone number last. Hold questions about parking or door codes until the booking, since those answers change nothing on the quote.\"}, {\"q\": \"How should a cleaning quote form handle commercial cleaning requests?\", \"a\": \"Give commercial work its own branch of questions. Ask for the square footage, the number of restrooms, the cleaning days each week, and the hours the building is empty. If a facility manager sends its own <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/rfp'>rfp form</a> instead, answer it with the same rates your form uses. Both quotes then agree.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a cleaning quote form show an exact price or a range?\", \"a\": \"Show an exact price when the answers describe the whole job, such as a recurring clean of a home with known rooms. Show a range, or no price, when the condition of the space decides the work, as with a first deep clean. Say on the form that the final price is confirmed at the first visit.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I add extras like inside the oven to a cleaning quote form?\", \"a\": \"Give each extra its own checkbox and a flat price, then let the form add the ones the customer ticks. Price each one from the time it takes your crew. Show the running total beside the list. The customer then sees what every extra adds before submitting.\"}, {\"q\": \"What happens after a customer submits a cleaning quote form?\", \"a\": \"The app saves the request with every answer and its quoted price, then emails the owner or posts in Slack. For a contract cleaning job, follow up with a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/proposal'>proposal form</a> that sets out the scope and the terms. With Emergent, each request lands in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"How long should a cleaning quote form be?\", \"a\": \"Keep it to the questions that move the price, which for a house clean is five to seven. Group them by topic, with the home first, then the schedule, then the extras. Forms built with Emergent have no response caps.\"}, {\"q\": \"When should a cleaning quote form ask for a walkthrough instead of giving a price?\", \"a\": \"Ask for one whenever the answers cannot tell you the condition of the space. Post-construction work and a first deep clean in months both fit. Put a short notes box beside those choices for the customer to describe the space before the visit.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a cleaning quote form ask about a one-time event?\", \"a\": \"Ask for the event date and the guest count, then whether you clean before the event or after it. Add a separate line for late-night work after the event ends. If the organizer offers sponsorship credit in place of payment, ask for their <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/sponsorship'>sponsorship form</a> and weigh its value against your quote.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
  "afb---how-to-step-6-des": "Send recurring requests to whoever schedules the regular crews and one-time jobs to the owner. A Slack channel suits a team that shares the work, and an email suits one person. Include the total the customer saw in every message.",
  "afb---prompt": "<p>Build a cleaning quote form for my house cleaning business that prices homes by bedrooms and baths.</p><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbPrompt = {\"default\": \"Build a cleaning quote form for my house cleaning business that prices homes by bedrooms and baths.\", \"chips\": [{\"label\": \"Price per Visit\", \"add\": \"Add the price per visit on screen before the customer submits.\"}, {\"label\": \"Cleaning Extras\", \"add\": \"Add cleaning extras such as inside the oven, each with its own price.\"}, {\"label\": \"Owner Alerts\", \"add\": \"Add owner alerts that email each new request with the quoted total.\"}, {\"label\": \"Walkthrough Flags\", \"add\": \"Add a walkthrough flag on any home over 4,000 square feet instead of a price.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
